[[:db/retract 17592186120459 :question/answer-fields 17592186118868] {:db/id 17592186119791 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-22790615-5765-50ce-b96c-1d82231be30c" "question-9a1ee2de-30e9-5dde-87e2-a6069fa7a03b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-22790615-5765-50ce-b96c-1d82231be30c" :question/id #uuid "22790615-5765-50ce-b96c-1d82231be30c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42668" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be a unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+y+z=-4 \\\\ y-2z=2 \\\\ 3x+2y+kz=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $y=6$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $7+4k,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=7+4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}| & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(2k+2)+4(0+6)+(0-6) \\\\  & =8k+8+24-6 \\\\  & =26+8k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{26+8k}{7+4k}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=6.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{26+8k}{7+4k} & =6 \\\\ 26+8k & =42+24k \\\\ 16k & =-16 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a46aaec-c335-5f1e-884c-19d1799ece0c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a46aaec-c335-5f1e-884c-19d1799ece0c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a46aaec-c335-5f1e-884c-19d1799ece0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49e9c67b-3d28-59fc-80d1-1d4cc0713555" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49e9c67b-3d28-59fc-80d1-1d4cc0713555" "answer-81135cf6-e842-57e1-aef8-392ad77737ec" "answer-e67665d0-ea97-55a9-9c9d-1d7010759bbe" "answer-3675aea5-a0c8-57f7-93a0-b11b85ed8248" "answer-0520e7af-36b0-5ef0-9563-eb7367b7cb27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49e9c67b-3d28-59fc-80d1-1d4cc0713555" :answer/id #uuid "49e9c67b-3d28-59fc-80d1-1d4cc0713555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81135cf6-e842-57e1-aef8-392ad77737ec" :answer/id #uuid "81135cf6-e842-57e1-aef8-392ad77737ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e67665d0-ea97-55a9-9c9d-1d7010759bbe" :answer/id #uuid "e67665d0-ea97-55a9-9c9d-1d7010759bbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3675aea5-a0c8-57f7-93a0-b11b85ed8248" :answer/id #uuid "3675aea5-a0c8-57f7-93a0-b11b85ed8248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0520e7af-36b0-5ef0-9563-eb7367b7cb27" :answer/id #uuid "0520e7af-36b0-5ef0-9563-eb7367b7cb27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119789 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4a38bcb4-0b4c-5b8b-bb9c-b7e3ce5c912c" "question-2a3030e8-5052-55cf-b8fe-d458398f5913"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a38bcb4-0b4c-5b8b-bb9c-b7e3ce5c912c" :question/id #uuid "4a38bcb4-0b4c-5b8b-bb9c-b7e3ce5c912c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42673" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+y=-3 \\\\ x-3y-2z=4 \\\\ -2x+y+2z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-14,$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+1y+0z=-3 \\\\ 1x+(-3)y+(-2)z=4 \\\\ (-2)x+1y+2z=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(15-4)-(-5+8)-3(1-6) \\\\  & =44-3+15 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{56}{-14}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f143de8-4808-52ba-8787-6ee60a482eb9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f143de8-4808-52ba-8787-6ee60a482eb9" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f143de8-4808-52ba-8787-6ee60a482eb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a30ac57b-8a8c-5c62-8fa8-59e9b44f8567" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4fc23eff-2e85-53ab-85d6-24718d451428" "answer-a30ac57b-8a8c-5c62-8fa8-59e9b44f8567" "answer-a379347f-b3fd-507c-a103-9d1da21b2d0c" "answer-cb8728d4-e8d5-5f53-8f10-8aeddf36b55b" "answer-e1a3b796-b620-52fb-a517-36825c287eea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fc23eff-2e85-53ab-85d6-24718d451428" :answer/id #uuid "4fc23eff-2e85-53ab-85d6-24718d451428" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a30ac57b-8a8c-5c62-8fa8-59e9b44f8567" :answer/id #uuid "a30ac57b-8a8c-5c62-8fa8-59e9b44f8567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a379347f-b3fd-507c-a103-9d1da21b2d0c" :answer/id #uuid "a379347f-b3fd-507c-a103-9d1da21b2d0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb8728d4-e8d5-5f53-8f10-8aeddf36b55b" :answer/id #uuid "cb8728d4-e8d5-5f53-8f10-8aeddf36b55b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1a3b796-b620-52fb-a517-36825c287eea" :answer/id #uuid "e1a3b796-b620-52fb-a517-36825c287eea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120459 :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-3z=7 \\\\ kx-4y+z=-19 \\\\ x-y-4z=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $z=-2$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $7k+23,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ k & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|=7k+23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $z$ is given by $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ k & -4 & -19 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -19 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -19 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-16-19)-(4k+19)+7(-k+4) \\\\  & =-70-4k-19-7k+28 \\\\  & =-61-11k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{-61-11k}{7k+23}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $z=-2.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-61-11k}{7k+23} & =-2 \\\\ -61-11k & =-14k-46 \\\\ 3k & =15 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-432aa278-91b8-5c39-89e2-129966c0aa56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-432aa278-91b8-5c39-89e2-129966c0aa56" :answer-field/id #uuid "432aa278-91b8-5c39-89e2-129966c0aa56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4d8e391-d9ee-52da-94f1-37df36eceaa0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7fe85483-816c-510e-9fd1-dd20c0b4191b" "answer-c108d1a2-60fc-5674-aa0a-d546a2379dfd" "answer-27fff04a-2bbe-5b26-ad65-edbd694ba9be" "answer-ee89842c-a371-5c4d-bdf4-656e2b69eca7" "answer-b4d8e391-d9ee-52da-94f1-37df36eceaa0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fe85483-816c-510e-9fd1-dd20c0b4191b" :answer/id #uuid "7fe85483-816c-510e-9fd1-dd20c0b4191b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c108d1a2-60fc-5674-aa0a-d546a2379dfd" :answer/id #uuid "c108d1a2-60fc-5674-aa0a-d546a2379dfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27fff04a-2bbe-5b26-ad65-edbd694ba9be" :answer/id #uuid "27fff04a-2bbe-5b26-ad65-edbd694ba9be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee89842c-a371-5c4d-bdf4-656e2b69eca7" :answer/id #uuid "ee89842c-a371-5c4d-bdf4-656e2b69eca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4d8e391-d9ee-52da-94f1-37df36eceaa0" :answer/id #uuid "b4d8e391-d9ee-52da-94f1-37df36eceaa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2a3030e8-5052-55cf-b8fe-d458398f5913" :question/id #uuid "2a3030e8-5052-55cf-b8fe-d458398f5913" :question/math-academy-id "q-73691" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-3y=1 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z=0 \\\\ y-z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-21,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+(-3)y+0z=1 \\\\ 5x+4y+(-2)z=0 \\\\ 0x+1y+(-1)z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{y},$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the second column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(0+6)-(-5-0)+0 \\\\  & =18+5 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{23}{-21}=-\\frac{23}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dc965890-90b8-58cc-bc3f-efeb4ad8684c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc965890-90b8-58cc-bc3f-efeb4ad8684c" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc965890-90b8-58cc-bc3f-efeb4ad8684c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-061ca3b9-19da-5830-8387-482e73317df9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73c24e43-321d-50e6-b1e7-cdf2748817be" "answer-061ca3b9-19da-5830-8387-482e73317df9" "answer-05e0253b-532c-58d8-b091-347993c3f893" "answer-b917f57a-83ba-5e72-bb47-0cffe8883bc7" "answer-489fa8d1-175b-5fa4-8798-bbe1b2637681"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73c24e43-321d-50e6-b1e7-cdf2748817be" :answer/id #uuid "73c24e43-321d-50e6-b1e7-cdf2748817be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-061ca3b9-19da-5830-8387-482e73317df9" :answer/id #uuid "061ca3b9-19da-5830-8387-482e73317df9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05e0253b-532c-58d8-b091-347993c3f893" :answer/id #uuid "05e0253b-532c-58d8-b091-347993c3f893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{23}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b917f57a-83ba-5e72-bb47-0cffe8883bc7" :answer/id #uuid "b917f57a-83ba-5e72-bb47-0cffe8883bc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-489fa8d1-175b-5fa4-8798-bbe1b2637681" :answer/id #uuid "489fa8d1-175b-5fa4-8798-bbe1b2637681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a1ee2de-30e9-5dde-87e2-a6069fa7a03b" :question/id #uuid "9a1ee2de-30e9-5dde-87e2-a6069fa7a03b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73695" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=-1 \\\\ x+5y+3z=k \\\\ 7x-3y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $z=-3$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-16,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $z$ is given by $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & k \\\\ 7 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(4-7k)-(-3-35) \\\\  & =-4+7k+38 \\\\  & =7k+34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{7k+34}{-16}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $z=-3.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7k+34}{-16} & =-3 \\\\ 7k+34 & =48 \\\\ 7k & =14 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d561005-378c-508e-a82e-2d8043716be1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d561005-378c-508e-a82e-2d8043716be1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d561005-378c-508e-a82e-2d8043716be1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e5a75d9-2669-5164-ae35-761e45c73242" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f73e832f-6af7-5391-9436-80207cb6c290" "answer-630877d4-1651-51d8-aadc-515dcd79b003" "answer-22a43538-527f-5e1c-8777-5a1b965cf68f" "answer-2e5a75d9-2669-5164-ae35-761e45c73242" "answer-8103e5b5-a679-5861-8dd6-741437678c88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f73e832f-6af7-5391-9436-80207cb6c290" :answer/id #uuid "f73e832f-6af7-5391-9436-80207cb6c290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-630877d4-1651-51d8-aadc-515dcd79b003" :answer/id #uuid "630877d4-1651-51d8-aadc-515dcd79b003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22a43538-527f-5e1c-8777-5a1b965cf68f" :answer/id #uuid "22a43538-527f-5e1c-8777-5a1b965cf68f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e5a75d9-2669-5164-ae35-761e45c73242" :answer/id #uuid "2e5a75d9-2669-5164-ae35-761e45c73242" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8103e5b5-a679-5861-8dd6-741437678c88" :answer/id #uuid "8103e5b5-a679-5861-8dd6-741437678c88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-71b4c62d-258c-5e6d-b466-361c4a8360c6" :activity/id #uuid "71b4c62d-258c-5e6d-b466-361c4a8360c6" :activity/title "Cramer’s Rule for 3x3 Systems" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 1759218604